<GovernanceLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How Commercial Roofing Intel builds its comparisons, decision tools, and datasets — data collection, analysis, assumptions, and limitations."
  crumbName="Methodology"
  lede="Numbers without methodology are marketing. This page explains how CRI's comparisons, tools, and datasets are built — and each one links back here plus its own specific methodology notes."
  updated="2026-07-15"
>
  <h2>Comparisons</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Comparison criteria are defined before evaluation begins and are identical for every option compared.</li>
    <li>Performance data comes from standards-body testing, manufacturer technical data sheets (not marketing), field research, and CRI datasets.</li>
    <li>Where options excel under different conditions, we present condition-based guidance rather than forcing a single “winner.”</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Decision tools</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every calculator and estimator publishes its inputs, formula or model logic, assumptions, and data vintage on an accompanying methodology section.</li>
    <li>Outputs are ranges with stated uncertainty, not false-precision point estimates.</li>
    <li>Tools are validated against published reference data before release and re-validated when underlying data updates.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Datasets</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each dataset page documents: data sources, collection method, sample size or coverage, time period, cleaning rules, and known limitations.</li>
    <li>Proprietary CRI data is aggregated and anonymized; no client- or building-identifiable data is published.</li>
    <li>Datasets carry version numbers and change logs so citations remain stable.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cost data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Cost figures state their region, year, and what is included (materials, labor, tear-off, disposal, etc.).</li>
    <li>National averages are presented only with ranges and regional caveats — roofing costs are local.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we won’t publish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Point estimates we cannot defend.</li>
    <li>Rankings without published criteria.</li>
    <li>“Best of” lists influenced by commercial relationships.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Questions about any specific methodology? <a href="/contact/">Contact the editorial team</a> —
    methodology challenges are treated with the same seriousness as
    <a href="/about/corrections/">correction requests</a>.
  </p>
</GovernanceLayout>
